$padsBody = Before-CTA $padsBody (Section 'Technical presentation' 'Filter Paper & Pad Deep Dive' '<div class="prose-grid"><div><p>Review the media families, pulp types, construction differences, published grade tables, high-temperature pads and activated carbon pads in this 10-page presentation.</p></div><aside class="note"><strong>Use as a product overview.</strong><p>Confirm current grade availability, tolerances and application suitability with Sri Bharathi before specifying a filter pad.</p></aside></div><div class="pdf-viewer"><object data="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf#page=1&amp;view=FitH" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Filter Paper and Pad Deep Dive presentation"><div class="pdf-fallback"><p>Your browser cannot show this PDF inline.</p><a href="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the presentation</a></div></object></div><p class="pdf-actions"><a class="button" href="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full screen</a></p>' 'section-muted')
New-Page '/filter-pads/' 'Industrial Filter Pads Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'Industrial filter pads from Sri Bharathi: cellulose pulp, sparkler, activated carbon and high-temperature pads, with an engineering selection guide.' 'Industrial Filter Pads for Process Clarification' 'Core product category' 'Sri Bharathi manufactures cellulose-based and application-specific filter pads for clarification, polishing and particulate-retention duties across industrial liquid processes.' $padsBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Pads','/filter-pads/')) 'Product' 'Industrial Filter Pads'

# Product pages
$sparklerBody = Product-Body -How '<p>A horizontal plate sparkler filter contains stacked plates with perforated support screens. Feed enters the closed shell under pump pressure and is distributed across the plate stack. The supported pad or cloth retains solids while filtrate passes through the media, enters the central interlocking-cup channel and leaves the filter.</p><p>As deposited solids form a cake, resistance rises and flow commonly falls at constant pump conditions. The useful cycle ends when throughput, differential pressure or filtrate quality reaches the agreed limit. Correct pad diameter, centre-hole geometry, sealing and flow direction are essential to prevent bypass.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi publishes disposable and reusable sparkler media in woven and nonwoven constructions. Referenced materials include polypropylene, nylon, cotton and polyester, with specialty fabrics available for particular duties. Heat-sealed or reinforced edges may be used to improve durability.</p><p>Media selection should account for chemical compatibility, temperature, slurry abrasiveness, required cake release, cleanability and the risk of fibre migration. Cellulose pulp pads may also be cut for supported sparkler duties where depth clarification is required.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Fits horizontal plate filters','Pads are cut around plate OD, centre opening and flow-path requirements to support proper sealing.',''),@('02','Clarification and cake support','The pad retains particles directly and supports the developing cake during batch filtration.',''),@('03','Multiple media families','Woven, nonwoven and cellulose-based options allow compatibility and retention to be balanced.',''),@('04','Disposable or reusable','The choice depends on validation, cleaning practicality, economics and contamination risk.',''),@('05','Edge reinforcement','Heat sealing or reinforcement can improve handling life on suitable synthetic constructions.',''),@('06','Custom converting','Final dimensions should follow an approved drawing or physical sample to prevent bypass.','')) -Specs @(@('Published materials','Polypropylene, nylon, cotton, polyester and specialty fabrics.','Match media chemistry and temperature to the process fluid.'),@('Construction','Woven and nonwoven; disposable and reusable options are referenced.','Controls flow, cake release, cleanability and particle retention.'),@('Dimensions','Made to equipment geometry; submit OD, ID, holes/notches and thickness.','Correct fit protects against edge or centre bypass.'),@('Operating limit','Grade-specific; not published as one universal value.','Confirm maximum differential pressure and temperature for the selected medium.'),@('Retention','Application- and media-specific.','Validate with the real suspension; woven cloth and depth pads behave differently.'),@('Change-out trigger','Pressure, falling flow, batch endpoint or filtrate-quality limit.','A defined endpoint improves repeatability and protects equipment.')) -Applications '<p>Sparkler filter pads are used extensively in pharmaceutical and chemical processing and can be evaluated for food, beverage, oil and gelatin clarification when material and document requirements are met. They are typically chosen for batch clarification, catalyst or particulate recovery, polishing and protection of downstream filters.</p><h3>Data needed for selection</h3><ul><li>Equipment make, plate diameter, centre-hole size and pad drawing</li><li>Fluid composition, pH, temperature and solvent exposure</li><li>Viscosity, solids concentration and approximate particle distribution</li><li>Target filtrate clarity, initial flow and acceptable cycle time</li><li>Disposable versus reusable preference and cleaning method</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Why does sparkler-filter flow decrease during a batch?','The retained solids form an increasingly resistant cake. Flow falls unless the pump raises differential pressure; operation should remain within equipment and media limits.'),@('Can a cloth and a cellulose pad be substituted directly?','Not automatically. They may differ in thickness, compressibility, sealing, retention, cake release and pressure-drop behaviour.'),@('What causes bypass in a sparkler filter?','Incorrect OD or centre-hole dimensions, damaged media, poor plate alignment, inadequate sealing, folds or an incorrect assembly sequence can allow unfiltered paths.'),@('Should sparkler pads be pre-wetted?','That depends on the media and process. If pre-wetting is used, the wetting fluid, volume and disposal or recovery procedure should be defined in the operating method.')) -Related '<a href="pulp-filter-pads.html">Cellulose pulp filter pads</a><a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Gelatin clarification</a><a href="../filter-papers/index.html">Industrial filter papers</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/index.html">Polishing cartridges</a>'
New-Page '/filter-pads/sparkler-filter-pads.html' 'Sparkler Filter Pad Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'Sparkler filter pads for horizontal plate filters: operating principle, media options, sizing, applications, troubleshooting and enquiry data.' 'Sparkler Filter Pads for Horizontal Plate Filters' 'Filter pads' 'Cut media for sparkler filter assemblies, selected around plate geometry, fluid compatibility, solids loading, clarification target and cycle economics.' $sparklerBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Pads','/filter-pads/'),@('Sparkler Filter Pads','/filter-pads/sparkler-filter-pads.html')) 'Product' 'Sparkler Filter Pads'

$pulpBody = Product-Body -How '<p>Pulp filter pads use a formed fibre network as a depth-filtration bed. Larger particles are intercepted near the upstream side while smaller particles follow tortuous paths into the sheet and are retained by mechanical interception and process-dependent interactions with the fibre matrix. A surface cake may contribute additional retention as the run proceeds.</p><p>Sri Bharathi groups its published pulp-pad range by rough or normal filtration, clarifying and polishing duties, and fine or premium filtration. Those descriptions are functional categories—not interchangeable micron claims. A trial should confirm clarity, throughput and pressure rise with the intended fluid.</p>' -Construction '<p>Published Sri Bharathi information describes virgin, unbleached pulp raw material and automated manufacture from pulping through finished media, with reduced direct handling. Existing company materials also reference wood pulp, cotton pulp and hybrid pulp constructions. Raw material and finished-media controls include filtration efficiency, pad porosity, absorbency, filtration speed and bursting factor.</p><p>Applicable fibres receive a porous, chemically inert wet-strength impregnation to improve mechanical strength in aqueous filtration. The exact furnish, impregnation and food-contact documentation must be confirmed for the ordered grade.</p><h3>Alpha-cellulose purity</h3><p>Alpha cellulose describes the relatively high-molecular-weight cellulose fraction that remains insoluble under a defined alkali test. It can be relevant to consistency, extractables and sensitive-use assessment. No public grade document was found that verifies 90% or 98% values for Sri Bharathi media, so those figures require written grade-specific confirmation before use.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Depth-loading fibre matrix','Particles can be retained through the sheet thickness instead of only at a single surface.',''),@('02','Multiple clarification levels','Published categories cover rough, normal, clarifying, polishing, fine and premium duties.',''),@('03','Monitored media properties','Porosity, absorbency, filtration speed, efficiency and bursting factor are listed process controls.',''),@('04','Wet-strength treatment','Applicable grades are impregnated to improve mechanical integrity during aqueous filtration.',''),@('05','Custom requirements','On-demand specification is referenced, subject to technical and manufacturing review.',''),@('06','Controlled conversion','Dimensions and openings can be matched to supported filtration equipment.','')) -Specs @(@('Raw material','Virgin, unbleached pulp is stated on the current product page.','Confirm furnish and contact documentation for the ordered grade.'),@('Fibre options','Wood pulp, cotton pulp and hybrid pulp are referenced in company materials.','Furnish influences formation, strength and process compatibility.'),@('Filtration category','Rough/normal, clarifying/polishing, fine/premium.','Use as a starting point; approve final performance by trial.'),@('Thickness / GSM','Legacy MMC guide: 0.5–2.5 mm and 250–1050 GSM; legacy MMCR guide: 1–3 mm and 500–1300 GSM.','Confirm current grade, nominal value, tolerance and test method.'),@('Porosity / filtration speed','Monitored parameters; grade values available through technical enquiry.','Influence pressure drop, throughput and cycle length.'),@('Strength','Bursting factor monitored; applicable grades use wet-strength treatment.','Important for saturated handling and supported pressure filtration.'),@('Alpha cellulose','Grade-specific documentation required; 90%/98% not publicly verified.','Relevant to purity assessment but not a stand-alone retention rating.')) -Applications '<p>Pulp pads can be evaluated for pharmaceutical intermediates, chemicals, cosmetics, beverages, food-process liquids, gelatin and compatible edible-oil duties. Selection changes with clarification stage: an open precoat or rough grade may protect a finer polishing grade, while a denser final pad may be used when incoming solids have already been reduced.</p><h3>Trial acceptance criteria</h3><ul><li>Filtrate turbidity or agreed visual/particle criterion</li><li>Initial and terminal flow at recorded differential pressure</li><li>Volume or mass processed before endpoint</li><li>Product loss during wetting, hold-up and change-out</li><li>Pad integrity, edge sealing and post-run appearance</li><li>Extractables, contact and traceability documents required by the application</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Are pulp filter pads the same as filter paper?','They are related cellulose media, but pads are typically thicker depth structures while papers may be thinner and used for fast or coarse filtration. The tested grade and equipment define the duty.'),@('Does higher alpha cellulose guarantee finer filtration?','No. Cellulose purity concerns material composition; retention also depends on fibre geometry, sheet formation, density, thickness, porosity and operating conditions.'),@('Why might a finer pad shorten batch time?','A finer or denser pad may blind sooner when upstream solids loading is high. Staged filtration or preclarification can improve the final polishing cycle.'),@('What should be supplied for a custom pad?','Provide a dimensioned drawing, equipment details, current sample if available, process conditions and required acceptance documents.')) -Related '<a href="sparkler-filter-pads.html">Sparkler filter pads</a><a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Gelatin filtration</a><a href="../filter-papers/index.html">Filter papers</a><a href="../lenticular-filters/index.html">Lenticular filters</a>'
New-Page '/filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html' 'Pulp & Cellulose Filter Pads Manufacturer | Sri Bharathi' 'Pulp and cellulose filter pads for industrial depth filtration, with guidance on furnish, alpha cellulose, porosity, strength and grade trials.' 'Pulp & Cellulose Filter Pads' 'Filter pads' 'Virgin-pulp depth media for rough filtration, clarification, polishing and fine filtration, manufactured with monitored formation and media properties.' $pulpBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Pads','/filter-pads/'),@('Pulp Filter Pads','/filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html')) 'Product' 'Pulp and Cellulose Filter Pads'

$carbonBody = Product-Body -How '<p>An activated carbon filter pad incorporates adsorptive carbon within a supported filter matrix. As a compatible liquid passes through the pad, suspended particles can be retained by the media while selected dissolved colour- or odour-causing compounds may adsorb onto available carbon surface.</p><p>This replaces two separate operations in some plate-and-frame or supported-pad processes: dosing loose powdered carbon into a tank and subsequently removing that powder on paper or cloth. Adsorption capacity is finite, so colour or odour breakthrough—not only differential pressure—can determine the endpoint.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi publishes carbon-impregnated pads made with different activated-carbon grades to help optimise the filtration duty. The detailed carbon type, loading, binder or support chemistry, dimensions and extractables profile are grade-specific and should be requested before trial.</p><p>Because adsorption is molecule-specific, an activated carbon pad cannot be selected solely by particle-retention language. Contact time, concentration, temperature, pH, competing organics, flow and carbon accessibility all influence treatment performance.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Adsorption plus filtration','Combines particulate retention with carbon-based reduction of selected dissolved compounds.',''),@('02','Contained carbon format','Can reduce loose-carbon dosing and the downstream task of capturing carbon powder.',''),@('03','Simplified handling','Pad form may reduce dust, tank clean-up and carbon scraping in compatible equipment.',''),@('04','Grade choice','Different carbon grades are referenced for optimisation of specific liquids.',''),@('05','Defined breakthrough','Colour, odour or analytical endpoint can be trended during a qualification run.',''),@('06','Cut-to-fit media','Dimensions should match the filter support and seal geometry to prevent bypass.','')) -Specs @(@('Functional component','Activated carbon incorporated in a filter pad.','Provides finite adsorption sites for compatible target compounds.'),@('Carbon grade / loading','Grade-specific; request declared information.','Drives adsorption behaviour, capacity and potential extractables.'),@('Retention','Depends on the supporting media and process.','Do not assume adsorption performance equals a particulate micron rating.'),@('Dimensions','Made for compatible supported-pad or plate-and-frame equipment.','Fit and sealing are essential to avoid untreated bypass.'),@('Operating conditions','Fluid-, carbon- and support-specific.','Confirm pH, solvent, temperature and differential-pressure compatibility.'),@('Endpoint','Breakthrough, pressure limit, batch volume or quality criterion.','Adsorption can exhaust even when the pad is not hydraulically blocked.')) -Applications '<p>Activated carbon pads may be considered where colour, odour or trace organic reduction is needed alongside clarification in compatible chemical, beverage, food and process-liquid duties. Suitability depends on whether the target compound adsorbs effectively and whether the pad materials meet product-contact requirements.</p><h3>Qualification approach</h3><ul><li>Define the target compound or measurable colour/odour criterion.</li><li>Record feed concentration, temperature, pH and flow per unit area.</li><li>Sample across the run to establish a breakthrough curve.</li><li>Measure any initial rinse requirement and product yield loss.</li><li>Check for carbon fines, extractables and interaction with valuable product components.</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Is an activated carbon pad equivalent to adding powdered activated carbon?','Not exactly. Carbon dose, accessible surface area, contact pattern and residence time differ. A side-by-side process trial is needed.'),@('Can activated carbon remove every colour or odour?','No. Adsorption is selective and affected by molecular size, polarity, pH, temperature and competing substances.'),@('When should an activated carbon pad be changed?','Use an agreed outlet-quality or breakthrough limit, together with pressure and throughput criteria. Pressure alone may not reveal exhausted adsorption capacity.'),@('Does the activated carbon pad eliminate downstream filtration?','It can combine functions in some systems, but a polishing filter may still be required depending on fines control and final cleanliness.')) -Related '<a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical filtration</a><a href="../applications/food-beverage-filtration.html">Beverage filtration</a><a href="pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP polishing cartridges</a>'
$carbonBody = Before-CTA $carbonBody (Section 'Technical presentation' 'Filter Pad and Activated Carbon Pad Overview' '<div class="prose"><p>The Filter Paper &amp; Pad Deep Dive includes media construction, published pad grades and a dedicated activated carbon pad overview. The inline viewer opens directly on the activated carbon pad section.</p></div><div class="pdf-viewer"><object data="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf#page=9&amp;view=FitH" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Activated carbon pad presentation"><div class="pdf-fallback"><p>Your browser cannot show this PDF inline.</p><a href="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf#page=9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the presentation</a></div></object></div><p class="pdf-actions"><a class="button" href="/assets/documents/filter-paper-and-pad-deep-dive.pdf#page=9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full screen</a></p>' 'section-muted')
New-Page '/filter-pads/activated-carbon-filter-pads.html' 'Activated Carbon Filter Pads Manufacturer | Sri Bharathi' 'Activated carbon filter pads combine depth filtration and adsorption for compatible colour and odour reduction duties. See selection and trial guidance.' 'Activated Carbon Filter Pads' 'Adsorptive media' 'Activated carbon-impregnated filter media for processes that may benefit from contained adsorption and particulate retention in a single supported pad.' $carbonBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Pads','/filter-pads/'),@('Activated Carbon Filter Pads','/filter-pads/activated-carbon-filter-pads.html')) 'Product' 'Activated Carbon Filter Pads'

$htBody = Product-Body -How '<p>High-temperature filter pads provide a porous depth medium for removing particulate matter from hot, compatible liquids. In frying-oil service, circulation through supported media retains suspended crumbs and degradation solids that would otherwise remain in the oil.</p><p>Sri Bharathi publishes an operating-temperature range of 180–250 °C for this product family. That range does not replace confirmation of the precise grade, support arrangement, exposure time, pressure and fluid chemistry for each installation.</p>' -Construction '<p>The current Sri Bharathi source describes these as technically advanced, heat-resistant depth-filtration media in various dimensions. It does not publish the exact fibre or binder formulation. That construction should therefore be confirmed on the quotation and grade documentation rather than inferred from standard cellulose pads.</p><p>At elevated temperature, dimensional stability, seal integrity, oxidation, pressure drop and safe handling become as important as particle retention. The filter assembly, piping, pump, valves and operator procedure must all be rated for the process.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Published hot-service range','The existing product page states 180–250 °C for compatible liquids and chemicals.',''),@('02','Depth particulate removal','A porous structure captures suspended material through the media thickness.',''),@('03','Cooking-oil duty','The product is specifically referenced for filtration of oil used in frying processes.',''),@('04','Multiple dimensions','Various sizes are available, subject to equipment and support review.',''),@('05','Process quality support','Removing suspended fatty or food residues can support oil-management procedures.',''),@('06','Application confirmation','Grade-specific composition and limits should be approved before hot operation.','')) -Specs @(@('Published temperature range','180–250 °C.','Confirm continuous versus intermittent exposure and actual grade limit.'),@('Duty','Hot edible cooking oils and other compatible liquids/chemicals.','Fluid compatibility must be verified; the range is not universal permission.'),@('Filtration mode','Depth filtration.','Supports solids capture within the medium and at the developing cake.'),@('Dimensions','Various; provide equipment drawing or pad sample.','Correct support and sealing are critical at elevated temperature.'),@('Material composition','Not stated on the public source page.','Request a grade-specific technical data sheet before approval.'),@('Change-out','Based on pressure/flow, clarity and safe operating procedure.','Hot-media handling requires a controlled cool-down and disposal method.')) -Applications '<p>The published primary application is particulate removal from hot cooking oils used in frying, including hotels, restaurants and the wider food industry. Other hot liquids or chemicals require an explicit compatibility review because temperature resistance alone does not establish chemical suitability.</p><h3>Safety and selection considerations</h3><ul><li>Maximum and normal fluid temperature, including start-up excursions</li><li>Fluid flash point and applicable plant safety controls</li><li>Housing and support-plate temperature and pressure rating</li><li>Oil viscosity at the actual filtration temperature</li><li>Solids type, concentration and required circulation rate</li><li>Cool-down, drainage, change-out and disposal method</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Can a standard cellulose pad be used at 200 °C?','Do not assume so. Use only a grade whose supplier has confirmed the construction and limit for the intended exposure.'),@('Is 250 °C suitable for every liquid?','No. It is the published product-family range. Chemical compatibility, pressure, exposure duration, supports and safety controls remain application-specific.'),@('What determines the change-out point in fryer-oil filtration?','Track flow or pressure together with visible solids, oil-quality indicators and the site operating procedure. Avoid relying on appearance alone.'),@('Are these pads food grade?','The legacy page describes them as food-grade safe, but customers should request current, grade-specific food-contact documentation for their jurisdiction and use.')) -Related '<a href="../applications/edible-oil-filtration.html">Edible-oil filtration</a><a href="pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="sparkler-filter-pads.html">Sparkler filter pads</a><a href="../contact/index.html">Confirm hot-service compatibility</a>'
New-Page '/filter-pads/high-temperature-filter-pads.html' 'High Temperature Filter Pads for Hot Oil | Sri Bharathi' 'High-temperature filter pads published for compatible hot liquids from 180–250 °C, including particulate removal from edible cooking oil.' 'High-Temperature Filter Pads' 'Hot-process filtration' 'Heat-resistant depth media for particulate removal from hot cooking oils and other compatible liquids, with a published product-family range of 180–250 °C.' $htBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Pads','/filter-pads/'),@('High-Temperature Filter Pads','/filter-pads/high-temperature-filter-pads.html')) 'Product' 'High-Temperature Filter Pads'

# Filter papers
$paperBody = Product-Body -How '<p>Industrial filter paper is a porous fibre sheet that supports fast or coarse filtration by allowing liquid to pass while retaining suspended matter at the surface and within the fibre network. A cake may form and become part of the filtration mechanism as solids accumulate.</p><p>Flow and retention must be considered together: an open sheet may deliver rapid throughput but retain fewer fine particles, while a denser sheet can improve clarification at the cost of higher resistance and shorter cycles under heavy solids load.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi states that its filter papers are manufactured from virgin wood pulps, including softwood or hardwood furnish. Premium grades may receive impregnation to balance wet strength and other properties for the intended filtration duty.</p><p>Published critical parameters include porosity, bursting factor, particle-retention character and flow rate. These properties should be tied to a test method and grade tolerance before purchasing decisions are made.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Virgin wood-pulp furnish','Softwood and hardwood pulps are referenced as raw-material options.',''),@('02','Fast or coarse filtration','The range is positioned for duties where throughput and gross solids removal are important.',''),@('03','Wet-strength options','Premium grades may be impregnated for aqueous strength and application fit.',''),@('04','Measured performance inputs','Porosity, bursting factor, retention character and flow rate are key specification fields.',''),@('05','Converted formats','Sheets, circles or equipment-specific cut shapes can be discussed against a drawing.',''),@('06','Trial-based approval','Actual fluid testing resolves the tradeoff between clarity, flow and sheet life.','')) -Specs @(@('Fibre source','Virgin softwood or hardwood pulp.','Fibre morphology influences formation, strength and permeability.'),@('Porosity','Legacy PPN guide: 5 sec (PPN 01), 7 sec (PPN 15), 10 sec (PPN 02).','Confirm the current test method and tolerance; relates to permeability and filtration speed.'),@('Bursting factor','Legacy PPN guide lists 4 kg/cm² for PPN 01, PPN 15 and PPN 02.','Confirm the current method and wet/dry basis; indicates mechanical robustness.'),@('Particle retention','Characterised by grade and process trial.','Not interchangeable with an absolute membrane rating.'),@('Flow rate','Grade- and fluid-specific.','Depends strongly on viscosity, pressure, area and solids loading.'),@('Impregnation','Premium grades may be treated for required properties.','Confirm chemistry, extractables and contact suitability.'),@('Dimensions','Application-specific converted sheets or discs.','Approved drawing reduces risk of bypass and fit errors.')) -Applications '<p>Industrial filter papers may be used in chemicals, pharmaceuticals, foods, beverages, cosmetics and general process filtration where a supported disposable sheet is appropriate. They can serve as gross particulate media, cake-support layers, prefilters or laboratory/process-development tools.</p><h3>How to compare grades</h3><ul><li>Test equal effective area under the same feed, temperature and pressure.</li><li>Measure initial flow and total throughput to the defined endpoint.</li><li>Compare filtrate clarity or particle result at several points in the cycle.</li><li>Inspect for tearing, edge bypass, fibre release and difficult cake removal.</li><li>Review contact, traceability and extractables documents before regulated use.</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Is filter paper specified only by GSM?','No. GSM indicates mass per area. Porosity, formation, thickness, fibre furnish, strength and treatment determine how the sheet behaves.'),@('What is bursting factor?','It is a measure related to resistance to rupture under a specified test. The value is meaningful only with its method, units and whether the sample is wet or dry.'),@('Why can laboratory flow differ from plant flow?','Viscosity, temperature, effective area, pressure, solids concentration and cake development may all differ between the test and production equipment.'),@('Can filter paper be reused?','These papers are generally treated as disposable media. Reuse would require a demonstrated cleaning, integrity and contamination-control procedure.')) -Related '<a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="../filter-pads/sparkler-filter-pads.html">Sparkler media</a><a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical filtration</a><a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Gelatin filtration</a>'
New-Page '/filter-papers/' 'Industrial Filter Paper Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'Industrial filter papers manufactured from virgin wood pulp for fast and coarse filtration. Learn about porosity, strength, flow and selection.' 'Industrial Filter Papers' 'Cellulose filtration media' 'Virgin wood-pulp filter papers for supported industrial filtration, where porosity, bursting strength, particle retention and flow must be specified together.' $paperBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Papers','/filter-papers/')) 'Product' 'Industrial Filter Papers'

# Cartridge hub and pages
$cartHub = @"
$(Section 'Portfolio' 'Liquid and dust cartridges by construction' (Cards -Items @(
@('01','PP pleated cartridges','Gradient-density microfiber media with high pleated area for compatible critical liquid duties.','<a href="pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated →</a>'),
@('02','Spun-bonded cartridges','One-piece 100% polypropylene depth media with progressive outside-to-inside retention.','<a href="spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html">Spun bonded →</a>'),
@('03','Wound cartridges','Controlled yarn winding around PP or stainless-steel cores for robust depth filtration.','<a href="wound-filter-cartridges.html">Wound cartridges →</a>'),
@('04','Stainless-steel cartridges','Reusable mesh, sintered or fibre-metal elements for high-temperature and differential-pressure duties.','<a href="stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html">Stainless steel →</a>'),
@('05','Dust-collection cartridges','Pleated polyester media with application-specific coatings for industrial air filtration.','<a href="dust-collection-filter-cartridges.html">Dust collection →</a>'),
@('06','Application matching','Compatibility, retention, pressure drop, geometry and cleaning determine the correct construction.','<a href="../contact/index.html">Request selection support →</a>')
)))
$(Section 'Selection framework' 'Do not compare cartridges by micron label alone' '<div class="prose-grid"><div><p>Nominal and absolute ratings describe different performance claims and require a stated test method. Pleated surface area, depth gradient, fibre diameter, pore stability and the incoming particle distribution all influence real separation performance.</p><p>Confirm cartridge length, outside and inside diameter, end connection, gasket or O-ring material, flow direction, housing fit, operating temperature, differential pressure and sanitisation or cleaning method. Fluid compatibility must include every wetted component—not only the filter medium.</p></div><aside class="note"><strong>Housing details prevent delays.</strong><p>Provide the housing model, tube-sheet or socket design, cartridge count, current end code and seal material when requesting a replacement.</p></aside></div>' 'section-muted')
$(Section 'Questions engineers ask' 'Cartridge selection FAQs' (Faqs -Rows @(
@('What is the difference between pleated and depth cartridges?','Pleated cartridges use folded media for high area and are often selected for defined polishing duties. Spun and wound depth cartridges distribute solids through a thicker matrix and can suit higher dirt loads.'),
@('What does DOE mean?','Double open end describes a cartridge open at both ends, normally sealed in the housing using separate gaskets or knife-edge arrangements.'),
@('Can nominal and absolute micron ratings be compared directly?','No. The claim must include the efficiency definition and test method. A nominal label without test context is not equivalent to an absolute-rated element.'),
@('When should stainless steel be selected?','Consider it where temperature, chemical exposure, differential pressure, backwashing or reuse exceeds the practical limits of polymeric media—subject to metallurgy and pore validation.')
)))
$(CTA 'Match the cartridge to the housing and process' 'Share housing geometry, current end configuration, seal material, fluid, temperature, flow, differential pressure, solids load and target retention.')
"@
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/' 'Filter Cartridge Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'Filter cartridge manufacturer in India supplying PP pleated, spun-bonded, wound, stainless-steel and dust-collection cartridges.' 'Industrial Filter Cartridges' 'Liquid and air filtration' 'Sri Bharathi supplies pleated, spun-bonded, wound, stainless-steel and dust-collection filter cartridges for compatible process duties and housings.' $cartHub @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/')) 'Product' 'Industrial Filter Cartridges'

$ppBody = Product-Body -How '<p>PP pleated cartridges arrange microfiber media in folds around a central core, creating more filtration area than a flat cylinder of the same length. Sri Bharathi describes a gradient-density structure that is more open on the outside and finer toward the inside, allowing larger particles to be captured upstream while finer layers perform final retention.</p><p>Flow passes through the pleated pack to the core and then to the clean side of the housing. The greater area can lower initial flux per unit area and increase useful throughput, subject to media rating, solids load and differential-pressure limits.</p>' -Construction '<p>Published construction is all polypropylene with a robust outer cage and thermally welded assembly, avoiding adhesives in the fluid path. The product page references nominal and absolute options, gradient-density microfiber media and a surface area above 0.5 m².</p><p>Polypropylene offers broad compatibility, but every fluid, temperature and concentration should be checked. Seal materials and sanitisation exposure also require confirmation.</p>' -Features @(@('01','All-PP construction','Media and structural components are described as polypropylene.',''),@('02','Gradient-density media','Open-to-fine layers distribute captured solids through the media structure.',''),@('03','Pleated surface area','Published area is more than 0.5 m², depending on configuration.',''),@('04','Thermally welded','Construction is described as welded rather than adhesively bonded.',''),@('05','Multiple end codes','DOE, 226 and 222 O-ring styles are available in flat or fin variants.',''),@('06','Wide application range','Published uses span pharmaceuticals, beverages, water, gelatin and fine chemicals.','')) -Specs @(@('Lengths','10, 20, 30 and 40 inches.','Match housing length and stacking requirements.'),@('Published micron options','0.1, 0.2, 0.45 and 1–50 µm; source wording also references 0.1–40 µm.','Confirm exact grade, rating type, efficiency and test method.'),@('Outside diameter','69 mm.','Verify clearance within the housing.'),@('Inside diameter','28 mm.','Relevant to core geometry and flow path.'),@('Surface area','More than 0.5 m².','Exact value depends on length and pleat pack.'),@('End configurations','DOE; Code 7F/7S (226); Code 3F/3S (222).','Match socket, locking and seal arrangement.'),@('Rating type','Nominal and absolute options are referenced.','Request the efficiency definition and validation data for the selected grade.')) -Applications '<p>Published applications include fine chemicals, pharmaceuticals, deionised water, RO pre-filtration, ophthalmic liquids, biological fluids, oral drugs, photographic processes, emulsions, gelatin and beverages including wine, beer, fruit juice and alcohol.</p><h3>Selection cautions</h3><ul><li>A 0.2 or 0.45 µm label is not by itself a sterility claim.</li><li>Confirm pressure-drop curves in the actual fluid viscosity and temperature.</li><li>Review polypropylene and seal compatibility with solvents, oxidisers and hot cleaning.</li><li>Use upstream clarification where heavy solids would rapidly blind fine pleats.</li><li>Request current grade-specific contact and validation documents where regulated.</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('Are these cartridges sterilising-grade filters?','No sterilising-grade claim should be inferred from micron size alone. That requires grade-specific bacterial-retention validation and controlled manufacturing documentation.'),@('Why use gradient-density media?','It can distribute particles by size through the structure, improving contaminant capacity compared with a single uniform fine layer.'),@('What is the difference between Code 7 and Code 3?','Code 7 uses a 226 O-ring connection; Code 3 uses 222. Flat or fin-end variants affect housing fit and orientation.'),@('Can PP cartridges filter gelatin?','Gelatin is a published application. The grade must still be selected around temperature, viscosity, preclarification and target retention.')) -Related '<a href="spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html">Spun-bonded prefilters</a><a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Gelatin filtration</a><a href="../applications/pharmaceutical-filtration.html">Pharmaceutical filtration</a><a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Cellulose depth pads</a>'
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html' 'PP Pleated Filter Cartridge Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'PP pleated filter cartridges in 10–40 inch lengths and multiple end configurations for pharmaceutical, water, beverage, chemical and gelatin duties.' 'PP Pleated Filter Cartridges' 'Filter cartridges' 'All-polypropylene pleated cartridges with gradient-density microfiber media, designed to combine defined retention options, area and contaminant capacity.' $ppBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/'),@('PP Pleated','/filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html')) 'Product' 'Polypropylene Pleated Filter Cartridges'

$spunBody = Product-Body -How '<p>Spun-bonded cartridges are formed by depositing polypropylene fibres into a self-supporting depth structure. Sri Bharathi describes a true gradient density from the outer to the inner surface. Feed flows outside to inside: coarser voids encounter larger particles first and finer inner zones progressively retain smaller material.</p><p>Captured particles remain within the depth matrix while filtrate passes to the core. This distribution can provide useful dirt capacity and low initial pressure drop in general pre-filtration and clarification duties.</p>' -Construction '<p>The published construction is 100% polypropylene fibre, continuously formed around a central moulded core or supplied in coreless versions. The process does not require binders, resins or lubricants, and the product is described as resistant to media migration under normal intended service.</p><p>One-piece lengths up to 1016 mm and more are referenced. Exact diameter, core, end connection, rating type and operating limit must be matched to the housing and fluid.</p>' -Features @(@('01','100% polypropylene','Broadly compatible material for many aqueous and chemical duties.',''),@('02','Binder-free formation','Published as free of surfactants, binders and adhesives.',''),@('03','Gradient depth','Progressive outside-to-inside structure supports staged particle capture.',''),@('04','Core or coreless','Construction can be selected around pressure and housing needs.',''),@('05','Broad diameter choice','Standard, big-blue and larger diameters are listed.',''),@('06','Custom lengths','Standard 10–40 inch and custom sizes are referenced.','')) -Specs @(@('Material','100% polypropylene fibres.','Confirm fluid, concentration and temperature compatibility.'),@('Lengths','10, 20, 30 and 40 inches; custom sizes available.','Match effective housing length.'),@('Micron options','0.5, 1, 5, 10, 20, 25, 50, 75 and 100 µm.','Confirm nominal/absolute basis and test method.'),@('Outside diameters','64 mm (2.5 in), 114 mm (4.5 in), 6 in and 8 in.','Select for housing clearance and required area.'),@('Inside diameters','25, 28 and 48 mm.','Match support core and end hardware.'),@('Configurations','DOE and Code 7 (226 O-ring).','Confirm gasket/O-ring and seating geometry.'),@('Construction length','One piece up to 1016 mm and more is referenced.','Reduces joints; verify handling and housing fit.')) -Applications '<p>Published applications include food and beverages, pharmaceuticals, fine chemicals, magnetic coatings, petrochemicals, cosmetics, water treatment, metal finishing and electronics. Spun media is commonly evaluated as a prefilter before finer pleated cartridges or as a general particulate-removal element.</p><h3>Selection factors</h3><ul><li>Incoming solids load and distribution</li><li>Target retention and acceptable downstream particle burden</li><li>Required initial flow at clean pressure drop</li><li>Housing diameter and length</li><li>Core need under differential pressure and temperature</li><li>Disposal, traceability and contact-document requirements</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('What does gradient density mean?','The outer structure is more open and becomes finer inward, helping distribute solids rather than loading only the outside surface.'),@('When is a core recommended?','A core can provide extra mechanical support where differential pressure, temperature or handling demands warrant it. Confirm the actual cartridge limit.'),@('Is polypropylene compatible with every chemical?','No. It has broad compatibility, but concentration, temperature, exposure time and seals must be checked.'),@('Can a spun cartridge replace a pleated cartridge?','Sometimes for pre-filtration, but the two constructions differ in area, rating precision and loading behaviour. Trial data should guide substitution.')) -Related '<a href="pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated cartridges</a><a href="wound-filter-cartridges.html">Wound cartridges</a><a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical filtration</a><a href="../applications/food-beverage-filtration.html">Food & beverage</a>'
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html' 'Spun Bonded Filter Cartridge Manufacturer | Sri Bharathi' '100% polypropylene spun-bonded depth filter cartridges in standard and custom sizes, with 0.5–100 µm published options.' 'Spun-Bonded Filter Cartridges' 'Filter cartridges' 'Binder-free polypropylene depth cartridges with a progressive outside-to-inside structure for contaminant capacity and general process pre-filtration.' $spunBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/'),@('Spun Bonded','/filter-cartridges/spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html')) 'Product' 'Spun-Bonded Filter Cartridges'

$woundBody = Product-Body -How '<p>Wound cartridges are made by continuously winding filtration yarn around a perforated core in a controlled pattern. The overlapping yarn creates tapered flow channels and a depth matrix. Feed moves from outside to inside, depositing larger particles in the outer zones while progressively finer pathways retain smaller material.</p><p>Winding tension, yarn type, core, density and pattern establish the filtration behaviour. A well-matched wound cartridge can offer robust dirt holding at economical cost in high-solids liquid duties.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi publishes polypropylene yarn with a polypropylene core and cotton yarn with a stainless-steel core. Raw materials are processed into controlled fibres and rovings before winding. Other combinations should not be assumed without quotation.</p><p>Core and yarn must both be chemically and thermally compatible. Cotton may suit selected oils, dilute acids, solvents and potable-liquid duties, while polypropylene is referenced for organic acids, oils, concentrated alkalis, water, solvents and electroplating solutions—always subject to compatibility review.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Controlled yarn winding','Creates a rugged depth structure with graded flow pathways.',''),@('02','High dirt holding','Depth loading supports particulate removal in demanding liquid services.',''),@('03','Long size range','Published lengths extend from 10 to 60 inches.',''),@('04','Material combinations','PP/PP and cotton/stainless-steel constructions are listed.',''),@('05','Broad diameters','Outside diameters from 58 to 200 mm are referenced.',''),@('06','Housing compatibility','DOE and Code 7 configurations are available.','')) -Specs @(@('Published constructions','Polypropylene yarn/PP core; cotton yarn/stainless-steel core.','Select both yarn and core around the fluid and temperature.'),@('Lengths','10, 20, 30, 40 and 60 inches.','Confirm actual housing effective length.'),@('Micron options','0.5–100 µm.','Request rating basis and efficiency.'),@('Outside diameter','58–200 mm.','Supports standard and high-capacity housing formats.'),@('Inside diameter','25 mm.','Check core and seal arrangement.'),@('Configurations','DOE and Code 7 (226 O-ring).','Match the cartridge socket and seal.'),@('Operating limit','Grade-specific; not publicly stated.','Confirm differential pressure, temperature and flow before use.')) -Applications '<p>PP wound cartridges are referenced for organic acids, oils, concentrated alkalis, water, organic solvents and electroplating solutions. Cotton wound constructions are referenced for vegetable oils, dilute acids, organic solvents, potable liquids and alkalis. These lists are starting points—not blanket compatibility guarantees.</p><h3>Why trial a wound cartridge?</h3><ul><li>Actual yarn swelling can change flow and retention.</li><li>Soft or deformable particles may penetrate differently from rigid test dust.</li><li>Pressure-driven channeling can occur if construction or support is unsuitable.</li><li>Product fibres or gels may blind outer layers prematurely.</li><li>Core chemistry can be as critical as the wound yarn.</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('What controls the micron rating of a wound cartridge?','Yarn properties, winding pattern, tension and density create the depth pathways. The published rating should be tied to a defined performance method.'),@('Why choose cotton with a stainless-steel core?','That combination may suit selected process fluids or temperatures where cotton is preferred and a strong corrosion-resistant core is appropriate.'),@('Can wound cartridges be cleaned and reused?','They are generally treated as replaceable depth media. Validated reuse is difficult because solids lodge inside the winding.'),@('What causes fibre release?','Incompatible chemistry, excessive differential pressure, weak yarn, poor winding or incorrect flow can contribute. Use the specified direction and limits.')) -Related '<a href="spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html">Spun-bonded cartridges</a><a href="stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html">Stainless-steel cartridges</a><a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical filtration</a><a href="../applications/edible-oil-filtration.html">Oil filtration</a>'
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/wound-filter-cartridges.html' 'Wound Filter Cartridge Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'PP and cotton wound filter cartridges in 10–60 inch lengths and 0.5–100 µm published options for demanding liquid filtration.' 'Wound Filter Cartridges' 'Filter cartridges' 'Controlled yarn-wound depth cartridges for economical particulate removal, high solids capacity and compatibility-led material selection.' $woundBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/'),@('Wound','/filter-cartridges/wound-filter-cartridges.html')) 'Product' 'Wound Filter Cartridges'

$ssBody = Product-Body -How '<p>Stainless-steel filter elements use stable metallic pores to retain particles while allowing fluid to pass. Cylindrical designs provide a simple robust surface; pleated designs increase area. Sintered mesh or random-fibre constructions bond contact points to stabilise the porous structure.</p><p>These elements are selected when temperature, differential pressure, chemical exposure, backflushing or reuse exceeds the practical limits of many polymer or fabric media. Performance still depends on pore construction, alloy, support layers and housing sealing.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi publishes stainless-steel wire mesh, sintered metal, random-fibre and sintered-fibre types in cylindrical or pleated configurations. Existing text lists SS 304 and SS 316, with SS 316 repeated; any requirement for SS 316L must therefore be explicitly confirmed rather than assumed.</p><p>Coarser support media can protect the primary filter layer. Bubble-point testing is referenced as a way to identify openings larger than the specified pore size in joints or seams.</p>' -Features @(@('01','High-temperature resistance','Metallic construction extends use beyond many polymer media limits.',''),@('02','Differential-pressure strength','Supported mesh and sintered structures can withstand demanding service.',''),@('03','Washable and reusable','Elements may be cleaned or backflushed using a validated procedure.',''),@('04','Stable pore geometry','Sintered constructions are designed to preserve pore structure.',''),@('05','No fibre migration','Metallic media avoid polymer or textile-fibre shedding.',''),@('06','Custom forms','Tubes, cartridges, discs, plain cylinders and pleated elements are referenced.','')) -Specs @(@('Published alloys','SS 304 and SS 316.','Confirm exact grade, certificate and corrosion compatibility.'),@('Media types','Wire mesh, sintered metal, random fibre and sintered metal fibre.','Construction determines pore stability, cleanability and pressure drop.'),@('Lengths','10, 20, 30 and 40 inches; custom sizes available.','Match housing and support requirements.'),@('Micron options','0.5, 1, 3, 5, 10, 20, 25, 50 µm and more.','Confirm test method and pore/rating definition.'),@('Diameters','64 mm OD; 28 mm ID.','Verify housing clearance.'),@('Connections','DOE, 226, 222 and 1-inch NPT/BSP.','Match socket, thread and seal design.'),@('Integrity test','Bubble-point testing is referenced.','Agree test fluid, method and acceptance criterion.')) -Applications '<p>Published uses include catalyst recovery, polymer filtration, cross-flow and gas filtration, analytical and medical devices, oil filtration, hot-gas filtration, aerosols, fuel and hydraulic oils, gas-liquid separation and RO pre-filtration.</p><h3>Cleaning and reuse</h3><p>A reusable element needs a controlled cleaning method matched to the contaminant and metallurgy. Define maximum backflush pressure, cleaning chemistry, temperature, drying, inspection, integrity test and retirement criteria. Reuse should be based on restored flow and verified integrity—not appearance alone.</p>' -Faqs @(@('Is stainless steel always chemically resistant?','No. Alloy selection must consider chlorides, acids, alkalis, temperature and crevice conditions. Request the exact metallurgy.'),@('What is a bubble-point test used for?','With a suitable wetting liquid, it can indicate the largest effective pore or reveal oversized defects in seams and joints under a defined method.'),@('When is pleating useful?','Pleating increases area within a given envelope, potentially reducing clean pressure drop and extending the cycle, but it can complicate cleaning.'),@('Can these elements be steam cleaned?','Only if the exact alloy, seals, joints and construction are rated for the temperature, pressure and repeated cycles.')) -Related '<a href="wound-filter-cartridges.html">Wound cartridges</a><a href="pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated cartridges</a><a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical filtration</a><a href="../contact/index.html">Request metallurgy confirmation</a>'
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html' 'Stainless Steel Filter Cartridge Manufacturer | Sri Bharathi' 'Reusable SS 304 and SS 316 filter cartridges in mesh, sintered, fibre, cylindrical and pleated configurations for demanding process filtration.' 'Stainless-Steel Filter Cartridges' 'Metal filter elements' 'Reusable metallic filter elements for high-temperature, high-differential-pressure and chemically demanding duties where polymer media may be unsuitable.' $ssBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/'),@('Stainless Steel','/filter-cartridges/stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html')) 'Product' 'Stainless-Steel Filter Cartridges'

$dustBody = Product-Body -How '<p>A dust-collection cartridge draws contaminated air through pleated media. Particles are retained mainly at the outer surface while clean air passes to the cartridge core. Pulse-jet or other cleaning reverses flow briefly to release the dust cake into the collector hopper.</p><p>Pleating fits a large filtration area into a compact envelope. Open pleat spacing and surface treatment influence cake release, pressure drop and cleaning-air demand.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi publishes 100% polyester spun-bonded media formed into a cylindrical pleated pack, supported by a metal core and encapsulated with metal end caps. Sponge-rubber sealing can provide positive fitment. The media is described as thermally bonded without a binding agent.</p><p>Available treatments referenced by the source include PTFE coating or lamination, aluminium or stainless-steel antistatic coatings and fire-retardant coating. The coating must be matched to the dust hazard and operating environment.</p>' -Features @(@('01','High area','Published filtration areas range up to 20 m².',''),@('02','Surface filtration','Pleated polyester supports dust-cake release and pulse cleaning.',''),@('03','Multiple treatments','Moisture/oil, antistatic, fire-retardant and sticky-dust options are referenced.',''),@('04','Open pleat spacing','Supports cleaning access and reduces dust bridging.',''),@('05','Retrofit potential','Pleated bags may replace some conventional bags without collector modification.',''),@('06','Multiple mount styles','Flange, three-lug and standard configurations are listed.','')) -Specs @(@('Base medium','100% polyester spun-bonded media.','Confirm temperature and chemical exposure.'),@('Length','300–1400 mm to customer requirement.','Match tube sheet, cleaning system and available clearance.'),@('Diameter','150, 225 and 325 mm.','Controls fit and filtration area.'),@('Filtration area','0.96–20.0 m².','Verify actual pleat geometry for the quoted element.'),@('Treatments','PTFE coating/lamination, aluminium or stainless antistatic, fire retardant.','Choose around dust release, moisture, static and combustibility risk.'),@('Mounting','Flange, three-lug and standard.','Provide drawing and sealing details.'),@('Cleaning','Application-specific pulse or reverse-air system.','Air pressure and frequency affect life and emissions.')) -Applications '<p>Published industries include pharmaceuticals, steel, power, powder coating, cement, chemicals, metals and minerals, and paints and pigments. Dust testing and hazard assessment are essential before selection.</p><h3>Combustible-dust caution</h3><p>Antistatic or fire-retardant media alone does not make a dust collector explosion safe. The site must assess dust explosibility, ignition sources, grounding, venting or suppression, isolation and applicable regulations with qualified specialists.</p>' -Faqs @(@('What does PTFE treatment change?','A coating or membrane can improve surface release, moisture/oil resistance or fine-particle control depending on construction. Confirm the quoted treatment.'),@('Does more media area always improve performance?','Not if pleats are packed so tightly that dust bridges or cleaning air cannot reach the valleys. Area, pleat spacing and cleaning must be balanced.'),@('Can a cartridge solve a combustible-dust hazard?','No. It is one component of a collector system. A formal dust-hazard and explosion-protection design is required.'),@('What dimensions are needed for a replacement?','Provide overall length, OD, ID, end-cap design, mount type, gasket dimensions, current media and collector model.')) -Related '<a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Chemical processing</a><a href="../contact/index.html">Send a cartridge drawing</a><a href="index.html">All filter cartridges</a>'
New-Page '/filter-cartridges/dust-collection-filter-cartridges.html' 'Dust Collection Filter Cartridge Manufacturer | Sri Bharathi' 'Pleated polyester dust-collection cartridges with multiple coatings, 300–1400 mm lengths and up to 20 m² published filtration area.' 'Pleated Dust-Collection Filter Cartridges' 'Industrial air filtration' 'Pleated spun-bonded polyester cartridges with application-specific surface treatments for compact industrial dust collection and pulse cleaning.' $dustBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Filter Cartridges','/filter-cartridges/'),@('Dust Collection','/filter-cartridges/dust-collection-filter-cartridges.html')) 'Product' 'Pleated Dust-Collection Filter Cartridges'

# Lenticular
$lenticularBody = Product-Body -How '<p>A lenticular module stacks annular depth-filter sheets around an internal drainage structure. Feed enters the housing, moves through the depth media and reaches clean-side channels that collect filtrate toward the central outlet. Multiple sheet layers provide substantial area within a sealed, compact assembly.</p><p>Compared with exposed plate-and-frame sheets, the enclosed module can simplify handling and reduce open-product exposure. It does not eliminate the need to control differential pressure, flow direction, venting, pre-wetting or sanitation.</p>' -Construction '<p>Sri Bharathi describes modular/lenticular systems as piles of depth pads separated by an in-built drainage structure. Dividers support individual sheets, help resist deformation during heat treatment and hot sanitation, and create multiple flow channels. Rigid external clips assist module handling.</p><p>Specifications and material-of-construction options are application-dependent. Sheet grade, module diameter, cell count, gasket, housing connection and sanitation limits should be frozen in an approved specification.</p>' -Features @(@('01','Enclosed depth sheets','Reduces open handling compared with manually dressed sheet stacks.',''),@('02','Internal drainage','Separators collect filtrate and support multi-directional flow.',''),@('03','Sheet stability','Dividers provide mechanical support during processing and heat exposure.',''),@('04','Compact area','Stacked annular sheets package useful depth-media area in a housing.',''),@('05','Safer handling','External clips help protect sheets during loading and unloading.',''),@('06','Configurable materials','MOC and module specifications can be matched to compatible applications.','')) -Specs @(@('Media format','Stacked annular depth-filter sheets.','Choose grade for clarification target and solids load.'),@('Drainage','Built-in separators and clean-side channels.','Supports filtrate collection and sheet stability.'),@('Module size / cells','Application-specific; not publicly listed.','Match housing, batch volume and required area.'),@('Material of construction','Multiple compatible options are referenced.','Confirm plastics, seals and sheet materials for the process.'),@('Heat treatment','Design addresses deformation during heat treatment/hot sanitation.','Request grade-specific cycle limits and validation.'),@('Operating direction','Housing- and module-specific.','Incorrect assembly or flow risks bypass or damage.'),@('Integrity / endpoint','Define by process and supplier data.','Trend pressure, flow and filtrate quality.')) -Applications '<p>Lenticular filtration can be considered for beverage, food, gelatin, pharmaceutical intermediate and chemical clarification where enclosed depth media, manageable module handling and compact area are valued. It is often positioned after bulk solids removal and before finer cartridges.</p><h3>Start-up and operation</h3><ul><li>Confirm orientation and seals before closing the housing.</li><li>Vent trapped air and wet the module using the approved fluid and procedure.</li><li>Raise flow gradually while monitoring differential pressure.</li><li>Collect or divert initial rinse volume according to process controls.</li><li>Stop at the validated pressure, flow or quality endpoint.</li><li>Drain and remove the module using appropriate exposure and handling controls.</li></ul>' -Faqs @(@('How is a lenticular filter different from a sparkler filter?','Both can use depth media, but a lenticular module encloses stacked annular sheets around drainage cells, while a sparkler filter uses individual pads or cloths on horizontal plates.'),@('Can lenticular modules be sanitised?','Some constructions are designed for compatible hot sanitation. Confirm the exact time, temperature, cycle count and fluid for the quoted module.'),@('What causes premature pressure rise?','High incoming solids, insufficient prefiltration, viscous or cold feed, too-fine media, air binding or excessive initial flux can contribute.'),@('Are lenticular filters final membrane filters?','They are depth filtration modules. A validated membrane may still be required where a downstream microbial-retention claim is needed.')) -Related '<a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp depth pads</a><a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Gelatin filtration</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated polishing</a><a href="../applications/food-beverage-filtration.html">Food & beverage</a>'
$lenticularBody = Before-CTA $lenticularBody (Section 'Technical presentation' 'Lenticular and Modular Filter Media' '<div class="prose-grid"><div><p>Explore the migration from conventional sparkler pads to Sri Bharathi modular/lenticular filtration, including flow paths, handling, throughput and system advantages.</p></div><aside class="note"><strong>System overview.</strong><p>This 18-page presentation covers conventional sparkler filtration, modular/lenticular flow paths, handling and system benefits.</p></aside></div><div class="pdf-viewer"><object data="/assets/documents/lenticular-and-modular-filter-media.pdf#page=1&amp;view=FitH" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Lenticular and Modular Filter Media presentation"><div class="pdf-fallback"><p>Your browser cannot show this PDF inline.</p><a href="/assets/documents/lenticular-and-modular-filter-media.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the presentation</a></div></object></div><p class="pdf-actions"><a class="button" href="/assets/documents/lenticular-and-modular-filter-media.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full screen</a></p>' 'section-muted')
New-Page '/lenticular-filters/' 'Lenticular Filter Manufacturer India | Sri Bharathi' 'Lenticular depth-filter modules with stacked sheets and internal drainage for enclosed clarification in food, beverage, gelatin, chemical and pharma duties.' 'Lenticular Depth Filter Systems' 'Modular filtration' 'Enclosed stacks of supported depth-filter sheets that provide compact area, stable drainage and practical handling for process clarification.' $lenticularBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Lenticular Filters','/lenticular-filters/')) 'Product' 'Lenticular Depth Filter Systems'

# Applications
function Application-Body([string]$Requirements,[string]$Stages,[array]$Considerations,[string]$Products,[array]$Faqs) {
    return @"
$(Section 'Process requirements' 'What the filtration duty must achieve' "<div class='prose'>$Requirements</div>")
$(Section 'Process design' 'A staged filtration approach' "<div class='prose'>$Stages</div>" 'section-muted')
$(Section 'Selection variables' 'Data that changes media performance' (Cards $Considerations))
$(Section 'Sri Bharathi portfolio' 'Related products for the filtration train' "<div class='related-links'>$Products</div>")
$(Section 'Technical questions' 'Application FAQs' (Faqs $Faqs) 'section-muted')
$(CTA 'Discuss the full process, not an isolated micron number' 'Share feed quality, temperature, viscosity, solids, batch volume, existing equipment, desired result and required quality documents so an appropriate trial sequence can be proposed.')
"@
}
$gelatinBody = Application-Body '<p>Gelatin manufacture creates a demanding clarification duty because the process liquid can be warm, viscous and sensitive to yield loss. Suspended tissue, mineral residues, fines and process aids must be reduced without imposing excessive pressure drop or holding valuable gelatin within the media.</p><p>Successful gelatin filtration balances four objectives: visible clarity or turbidity, contaminant removal, acceptable throughput and product recovery. Temperature control is important because viscosity rises as gelatin solution cools, sharply increasing pressure drop and the tendency to gel within equipment.</p><h3>Why cellulose filter pads are used</h3><p>Cellulose depth pads provide a tortuous, porous network that can retain a broad distribution of fine suspended matter and build a clarifying cake. They can be cut for sparkler presses or incorporated in lenticular modules. Their useful dirt capacity makes them practical after bulk solids removal and before finer polishing cartridges.</p>' '<h3>1. Bulk solids removal</h3><p>Screening, settling or a suitably open filter stage protects clarification media from coarse particles and fibres.</p><h3>2. Depth clarification</h3><p>Pulp or cellulose pads capture suspended fines through sheet thickness. Sparkler filter pads suit installed horizontal plate equipment; lenticular modules provide an enclosed sheet format.</p><h3>3. Polishing</h3><p>A compatible PP pleated cartridge may reduce the remaining particle burden and protect downstream processing. A nominal or absolute label must be supported by the required efficiency data.</p><h3>4. Verification</h3><p>Trend temperature, pressure, flow, turbidity or agreed clarity, cycle volume and recovered yield. Trial at representative concentration because water testing does not reproduce gelatin viscosity or solids behaviour.</p>' @(@('01','Temperature and viscosity','Record both throughout the run; cooling can dominate pressure rise and gel risk.',''),@('02','Solids distribution','Coarse fibres, fines and soft particles load depth media differently.',''),@('03','Target clarity','Define turbidity, visual standard or analytical particle criterion.',''),@('04','Product yield','Measure hold-up, flush recovery and gelatin retained in spent media.',''),@('05','Media purity','Request fibre furnish, alpha-cellulose and extractables information for the actual grade.',''),@('06','Sanitation and documents','Define cleaning, contact and traceability requirements before approval.','')) '<a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Cellulose pulp filter pads</a><a href="../filter-pads/sparkler-filter-pads.html">Sparkler filter pads</a><a href="../lenticular-filters/index.html">Lenticular depth filters</a><a href="../filter-papers/index.html">Filter papers</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated cartridges</a>' @(@('What is the best micron rating for gelatin filtration?','There is no universal value. Feed solids, viscosity, temperature, stage objective and rating method must be defined. A staged trial is more reliable than choosing from a nominal number.'),@('Why does gelatin filtration slow down suddenly?','Cooling and concentration can raise viscosity or start gel formation; a loaded cake or too-fine medium can compound the pressure rise.'),@('Can cellulose purity affect gelatin processing?','Purity can be relevant to extractables and media consistency, but it does not independently define clarity. Request grade-specific alpha-cellulose data and test method.'),@('Should a fine cartridge be used first?','Usually heavy solids should be reduced upstream. Sending unclarified gelatin directly to a fine pleated cartridge can produce short cycles and high cost.'),@('How can yield loss be reduced?','Minimise unnecessary hold-up, size the system appropriately, optimise pre-wet/flush recovery and stop before gel blocks drainage—within the validated process.'))
New-Page '/applications/gelatin-filtration.html' 'Gelatin Filtration & Cellulose Filter Pads | Sri Bharathi' 'Technical guide to gelatin clarification using cellulose filter pads, sparkler media, lenticular filters and PP cartridges, with trial and selection criteria.' 'Gelatin Filtration & Clarification' 'Application guide' 'A technical approach to gelatin filter-media selection, staged clarification, temperature control, throughput and yield using cellulose depth pads and compatible cartridges.' $gelatinBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Applications','/applications/gelatin-filtration.html'),@('Gelatin Filtration','/applications/gelatin-filtration.html')) 'Article' 'Gelatin Filtration and Clarification'

$pharmaBody = Application-Body '<p>Pharmaceutical filtration can range from coarse clarification of intermediates to pre-filtration ahead of validated final membranes. The filtration objective, product-contact status and contamination controls must be explicitly defined; the presence of a fine micron label does not create a sterile or validated process.</p><p>Media selection should control visible and sub-visible particulate while meeting chemical compatibility, extractables, fibre release, traceability and batch-record needs. Process development should include differential pressure, flow, yield and integrity acceptance criteria.</p>' '<p>Use open depth media or cartridges to remove heavy suspended solids, then a clarifying pulp pad or lenticular module where broad particle loading is expected. A PP pleated cartridge may provide a defined polishing stage. If microbial retention is required, a separately validated membrane and process are normally needed downstream.</p><p>Each change of media, supplier, sanitisation cycle or operating condition should be evaluated through the site change-control and qualification system.</p>' @(@('01','Filtration objective','Clarification, bioburden reduction and sterilising filtration are different claims.',''),@('02','Product compatibility','Assess pH, solvents, actives, temperature and exposure duration.',''),@('03','Extractables','Request grade-specific data appropriate to product risk.',''),@('04','Retention evidence','Define nominal/absolute efficiency and required test method.',''),@('05','Batch traceability','Agree certificates, lot identification and change notification.',''),@('06','Sanitation','Confirm media and seal limits for rinse, hot water, steam or chemicals.','')) '<a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="../lenticular-filters/index.html">Lenticular filters</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated cartridges</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html">Stainless-steel elements</a>' @(@('Does a 0.2 µm cartridge guarantee sterility?','No. Sterilising-grade performance requires grade-specific validation against an appropriate microbial challenge and a controlled process.'),@('What documents should be requested?','Depending on risk: technical data sheet, material declaration, lot certificate, contact statements, extractables information, change notification and relevant validation data.'),@('Why use depth media before a membrane?','Depth media can remove a broad solids load and protect the more precise downstream membrane, extending service life.'),@('Can filter pads be used for APIs?','Potentially, but compatibility, product loss, extractables, cleaning and regulatory documentation must be assessed for the exact grade and process.'))
New-Page '/applications/pharmaceutical-filtration.html' 'Pharmaceutical Filtration Media | Sri Bharathi' 'Pharmaceutical clarification and pre-filtration using filter pads, lenticular media and cartridges, with compatibility and validation considerations.' 'Pharmaceutical Filtration Media' 'Application guide' 'Depth pads, enclosed sheet modules and cartridges for pharmaceutical clarification and pre-filtration, selected within the user''s validated quality system.' $pharmaBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Applications','/applications/pharmaceutical-filtration.html'),@('Pharmaceutical','/applications/pharmaceutical-filtration.html')) 'Article' 'Pharmaceutical Filtration Media Selection'

$chemicalBody = Application-Body '<p>Chemical filtration duties vary from removal of reactor solids and catalysts to polishing before packaging or protection of downstream equipment. A media recommendation begins with complete fluid composition—including minor solvents, oxidisers and cleaning chemicals—because compatibility can change sharply with concentration and temperature.</p><p>Viscosity, solids abrasiveness, particle shape and valuable-product recovery affect whether a pad, wound depth cartridge, spun cartridge, pleated element or reusable stainless-steel filter is most appropriate.</p>' '<p>Start with bulk solids removal where needed, then use a depth stage for variable fine-particle loading. Activated carbon pads can be trialled where a confirmed adsorbable colour or odour compound is present. Pleated cartridges provide polishing, while stainless-steel elements suit selected high-temperature, high-pressure or reusable duties.</p><p>For batch processes, define endpoint by filtrate quality and pressure/flow. For continuous service, include duty/standby capacity and a safe change-out or backwash strategy.</p>' @(@('01','Complete chemistry','Include solvents, pH, concentration, oxidisers and cleaning agents.',''),@('02','Temperature','Compatibility and viscosity can change at process temperature.',''),@('03','Solids character','Hard catalyst, soft agglomerates and gels load media differently.',''),@('04','Pressure profile','Record clean and terminal differential pressure.',''),@('05','Product recovery','Assess hold-up, flushing and valuable solids or filtrate recovery.',''),@('06','Disposal or cleaning','Select single-use depth media or validated reusable metal elements.','')) '<a href="../filter-pads/activated-carbon-filter-pads.html">Activated carbon pads</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/spun-bonded-filter-cartridges.html">Spun-bonded cartridges</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/wound-filter-cartridges.html">Wound cartridges</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html">Stainless-steel filters</a>' @(@('How is chemical compatibility confirmed?','Review every wetted material against the full formulation at actual temperature and concentration, then trial where interaction data is uncertain.'),@('When is activated carbon useful?','When the target dissolved compound is demonstrably adsorbed under the process pH, temperature, concentration and contact time.'),@('Why select stainless steel?','It may suit temperatures, pressures, solvents or cleaning cycles that challenge polymer media, provided the selected alloy resists corrosion.'),@('What causes short cartridge life?','High solids, gels, precipitation after cooling, too-fine prefiltration, excessive flux or chemical swelling can all contribute.'))
New-Page '/applications/chemical-filtration.html' 'Chemical Filtration Media & Cartridges | Sri Bharathi' 'Chemical filtration using depth pads, activated carbon, wound, spun, pleated and stainless-steel media selected for compatibility and solids load.' 'Chemical Filtration Media' 'Application guide' 'Compatibility-led filter pads and cartridges for catalyst removal, clarification, colour reduction and polishing in chemical process streams.' $chemicalBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Applications','/applications/chemical-filtration.html'),@('Chemical','/applications/chemical-filtration.html')) 'Article' 'Chemical Filtration Media Selection'

$foodBody = Application-Body '<p>Food and beverage clarification must balance visual quality, flavour and aroma preservation, throughput, yield and hygiene. Incoming solids may include pulp, haze-forming particles, processing aids or precipitated material. A staged approach protects fine media and makes batch performance more repeatable.</p><p>Product-contact documentation is grade-specific. Customers should request the current declarations required for the product and market rather than treating a general &ldquo;food grade&rdquo; phrase as universal approval.</p>' '<p>Coarse screening or settling can remove bulk matter. Pulp pads, sparkler media or lenticular sheets then provide depth clarification. Activated carbon pads may be evaluated for selected colour or odour compounds, while PP pleated cartridges can polish clarified liquid before filling or a further validated barrier.</p><p>Temperature, dissolved gas and product composition should be maintained during trials so sensory and throughput results represent production.</p>' @(@('01','Product quality target','Define turbidity, colour, flavour, aroma and shelf-life relevance.',''),@('02','Yield','Measure product retained in wet media and equipment hold-up.',''),@('03','Temperature/viscosity','Control both to make pressure and flow comparisons meaningful.',''),@('04','Contact documentation','Request declarations for the exact media and intended market.',''),@('05','Microbial objective','Clarification is not the same as validated microbial retention.',''),@('06','Cleaning and change-out','Design hygienic handling around housing and media format.','')) '<a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="../filter-pads/activated-carbon-filter-pads.html">Activated carbon pads</a><a href="../lenticular-filters/index.html">Lenticular filters</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/pp-pleated-filter-cartridges.html">PP pleated cartridges</a>' @(@('Will finer media always improve beverage quality?','Not necessarily. It may remove desirable components, reduce yield or blind rapidly. Define the actual quality objective and trial staged options.'),@('Can activated carbon pads affect flavour?','Yes. Activated carbon may adsorb desirable as well as undesirable compounds. Sensory and analytical trials are important.'),@('What is needed for food-contact approval?','Request current, grade-specific composition and compliance documents applicable to the jurisdiction and conditions of use.'),@('How can product loss be minimised?','Optimise area, pre-wetting, displacement or recovery volume, change-out endpoint and equipment drainage within hygienic process controls.'))
New-Page '/applications/food-beverage-filtration.html' 'Food & Beverage Filtration Media | Sri Bharathi' 'Filter pads, activated carbon media, lenticular filters and PP cartridges for food and beverage clarification, polishing and process yield.' 'Food & Beverage Filtration' 'Application guide' 'Depth and cartridge filtration for clarification and polishing of compatible food-process liquids and beverages, with attention to sensory quality, yield and hygiene.' $foodBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Applications','/applications/food-beverage-filtration.html'),@('Food & Beverage','/applications/food-beverage-filtration.html')) 'Article' 'Food and Beverage Filtration'

$oilBody = Application-Body '<p>Edible-oil filtration removes suspended food residues, fines and other particulate matter that can accelerate quality deterioration or interfere with downstream processing. Hot frying-oil duties add temperature, oxidation and operator-safety constraints. Viscosity falls as oil is heated, improving flow, but every component must be rated for the actual temperature.</p><p>Sri Bharathi publishes high-temperature depth pads for compatible operating temperatures from 180 to 250 °C. Standard pulp, paper, fabric, wound or stainless-steel media require separate temperature and compatibility confirmation.</p>' '<p>Use strainers or settling for coarse crumbs, followed by supported depth media for fine particulate capture. Where the process runs hot, select a specifically confirmed high-temperature pad and suitable filter hardware. Wound or stainless-steel cartridges may fit cooler polishing or utility-oil duties depending on construction.</p><p>Trend oil temperature, flow, differential pressure, visible solids and the site&rsquo;s oil-quality indicators. Establish safe isolation, drainage, cooling and spent-media handling.</p>' @(@('01','Actual temperature','Record normal, start-up and upset values at the filter inlet.',''),@('02','Oil viscosity','Use process-temperature viscosity for pressure-drop sizing.',''),@('03','Solids load','Crumbs and degraded fines influence depth-pad cycle length.',''),@('04','Food-contact documents','Confirm exact grade and conditions of intended use.',''),@('05','Fire and burn safety','Rate the entire system and define controlled hot-media handling.',''),@('06','Oil-quality endpoint','Combine filtration data with the plant oil-management programme.','')) '<a href="../filter-pads/high-temperature-filter-pads.html">High-temperature filter pads</a><a href="../filter-pads/pulp-filter-pads.html">Pulp filter pads</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/wound-filter-cartridges.html">Wound cartridges</a><a href="../filter-cartridges/stainless-steel-filter-cartridges.html">Stainless-steel filters</a>' @(@('What temperature range is published for Sri Bharathi hot-oil pads?','The current source states 180–250 °C for the product family. Confirm the exact grade, exposure and equipment before use.'),@('Does filtration restore used oil completely?','No. Filtration removes suspended particulate but does not reverse all chemical degradation or remove every dissolved oxidation product.'),@('Why filter oil hot?','Lower viscosity can improve flow and suspended solids are easier to circulate, but elevated temperature increases equipment and operator-safety requirements.'),@('Can standard paper be used in hot frying oil?','Only if the exact paper grade and support have been confirmed for the temperature and fluid. Do not infer suitability from appearance.'))
New-Page '/applications/edible-oil-filtration.html' 'Edible Oil Filtration & Hot Oil Filter Pads | Sri Bharathi' 'Edible and frying-oil filtration using high-temperature depth pads, with a published 180–250 °C range and practical process considerations.' 'Edible Oil Filtration' 'Application guide' 'Particulate removal from edible and frying oils using compatible depth media, including a high-temperature pad family published for 180–250 °C.' $oilBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Applications','/applications/edible-oil-filtration.html'),@('Edible Oil','/applications/edible-oil-filtration.html')) 'Article' 'Edible Oil Filtration'

# About, quality, certificates, resources, contact
$aboutBody = @"
$(Section 'Company' 'Filtration experience grounded in industrial practice' '<div class="prose-grid"><div><p>Sri Bharathi Tech Private Limited is part of the Sri Bharathi Group of Companies. Its filtration division manufactures and supplies sparkler pulp filter pads, filter papers, lenticular systems and multiple cartridge constructions for chemical, pharmaceutical, beverage, distillery, food and other process industries.</p><p>Existing company information describes a founder with more than 40 years of industrial experience, supported by research, development and custom specification work. The current portfolio includes wood-pulp, cotton-pulp and hybrid-pulp pads; PP pleated, spun-bonded and wound cartridges; stainless-steel elements; and pleated dust collectors.</p></div><aside class="note"><strong>How we approach a new duty</strong><p>We begin with process conditions, filter geometry and the required result. This narrows a trial candidate and the documents needed for technical approval.</p></aside></div>')
$(Section 'Operating values' 'Useful filtration starts with honest specification' (Cards -Items @(
@('01','Application fit','Recommendations are based on fluid, temperature, solids, equipment and quality target.',''),
@('02','Customisation','Dimensions and selected media parameters can be reviewed against user drawings and samples.',''),
@('03','Process control','Published controls include porosity, filtration speed, absorbency, efficiency and bursting factor.',''),
@('04','Evidence over slogans','Unverified ratings, approvals and alpha-cellulose figures are not published as facts.',''),
@('05','Technical continuity','Related pads, papers, modules and cartridges can be considered as one filtration train.',''),
@('06','Responsive support','Pune headquarters plus published regional addresses in Gujarat, Telangana and Kerala.','')
)))
$(Section 'More about Sri Bharathi' 'Quality and documentation' '<div class="related-links"><a href="quality.html">Quality approach</a><a href="certifications.html">Certification documents</a><a href="../resources/index.html">Technical resources</a><a href="../contact/index.html">Contact the team</a></div>' 'section-muted')
"@
New-Page '/about/' 'About Sri Bharathi Filtration Division' 'Learn about Sri Bharathi Tech Private Limited, its industrial filtration portfolio, manufacturing focus, technical approach and regional presence in India.' 'About Sri Bharathi Filtration Division' 'Company' 'An Indian manufacturer and supplier of industrial filter pads, papers, cartridges and lenticular systems, focused on process fit, controlled media properties and custom requirements.' $aboutBody @(@('Home','/'),@('About','/about/'))

$qualityBody = @"
$(Section 'Control points' 'From raw material to converted filtration media' '<div class="prose"><p>Sri Bharathi''s published manufacturing information describes virgin pulp inputs, automated filter-pad production and reduced direct handling from pulping to finished media. Raw materials are monitored and routine tests are stated for filtration efficiency, pad porosity, absorbency, filtration speed and bursting factor.</p><p>Applicable paper and pad fibres receive a porous, chemically inert wet-strength treatment intended to preserve mechanical strength during aqueous filtration. The relevant grade specification should identify which controls apply and how acceptance is recorded.</p></div>')
$(Section 'Qualification' 'What a useful quality package should contain' (Cards -Items @(
@('01','Approved specification','Media, dimensions, tolerances and declared performance tied to a product code.',''),
@('02','Test methods','Units and procedures for porosity, strength, flow or retention claims.',''),
@('03','Lot traceability','Manufacturing identification linked to release documentation.',''),
@('04','Material declarations','Grade-specific fibre, polymer, alloy and contact information as applicable.',''),
@('05','Change control','Agreed communication for material or process changes affecting the approved grade.',''),
@('06','Application trial','Documented performance in the user''s representative process before routine supply.','')
)) 'section-muted')
$(Section 'Customer responsibility' 'Confirm suitability in the real process' '<div class="prose"><p>Published catalogue values narrow product choice; they do not replace user qualification. Customers should verify compatibility, retention, extractables, microbial requirements, pressure, temperature, cleaning and applicable regulatory obligations.</p><p>For sensitive applications, request the latest technical data sheet and supporting documents with the quotation. Define any certificate fields or acceptance limits before the first production order.</p></div>')
$(CTA 'Build the required quality package into the enquiry' 'Tell us the product code or intended grade, application, market, contact conditions and documents required by your quality system.')
"@
New-Page '/about/quality.html' 'Filtration Media Quality Approach | Sri Bharathi' 'Sri Bharathi filtration media quality approach: raw-material monitoring, pad process controls, strength, porosity, traceability and user qualification.' 'Quality Approach for Filtration Media' 'Quality' 'A practical quality framework covering raw-material control, media-property testing, lot documentation and qualification in the customer&rsquo;s actual process.' $qualityBody @(@('Home','/'),@('About','/about/'),@('Quality','/about/quality.html'))

$certBody = @"
$(Section 'Document status' 'Current evidence comes before certification claims' '<div class="prose-grid"><div><p>The legacy Sri Bharathi website references an &ldquo;ISO 9001-2000 Certified manufacturing unit&rdquo; and a Dun &amp; Bradstreet certified manufacturing unit. ISO 9001:2000 is a superseded edition, and no current certificate file, scope, certificate number, issuer or validity date was publicly available during this website rebuild.</p><p>For accuracy, this new site does not present those legacy statements as current certifications. Customers should request controlled copies of current documents and verify the legal entity, manufacturing location, scope, issuing body and expiry date before relying on them.</p></div><aside class="note"><strong>No implied product approval</strong><p>A management-system certificate does not automatically certify every filter grade for food, pharmaceutical, sterile or other regulated use.</p></aside></div>')
$(Section 'Due diligence' 'What to verify on a certificate' (Cards -Items @(
@('01','Legal entity','The named organisation should match the contracting or manufacturing entity.',''),
@('02','Site and scope','Check that the relevant plant and filtration activities are within scope.',''),
@('03','Standard edition','Confirm the current standard and any applicable transition status.',''),
@('04','Issuer','Verify accreditation and certificate authenticity with the issuing body.',''),
@('05','Validity','Review issue, expiry and surveillance status.',''),
@('06','Product documents','Obtain separate grade-specific contact, material or validation evidence.','')
)) 'section-muted')
$(Section 'Request documents' 'Tell us what your approval process needs' '<div class="prose"><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@sribharathi.com">info@sribharathi.com</a> with the product or intended application, destination market and required document list. Sri Bharathi can then confirm which current documents are available for the specific supply.</p></div>')
"@
New-Page '/about/certifications.html' 'Certifications & Quality Documents | Sri Bharathi' 'How to request and verify current Sri Bharathi certification and product-quality documents without relying on outdated or unverified claims.' 'Certifications & Quality Documents' 'Document control' 'A transparent guide to requesting current, scope-specific company and product documentation for filtration-media qualification.' $certBody @(@('Home','/'),@('About','/about/'),@('Certifications','/about/certifications.html'))

$resourcesBody = @"
<section class="section" id="depth-filtration"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Technical note 01</p><h2>Understanding depth filtration</h2><div class="prose"><p>A depth medium is a three-dimensional porous network. Particles are retained within the media and at the upstream cake, so performance changes as loading progresses. Initial pressure drop, pressure rise, filtrate clarity and total throughput are more informative together than any single catalogue property.</p><h3>Parameters that are related but not interchangeable</h3><ul><li><strong>Thickness:</strong> physical sheet depth; it can influence holding capacity and equipment fit.</li><li><strong>GSM:</strong> media mass per square metre; not a direct micron rating.</li><li><strong>Porosity/permeability:</strong> ease of fluid passage under a defined method.</li><li><strong>Wet and dry strength:</strong> resistance to handling and rupture before and after saturation.</li><li><strong>Retention:</strong> fraction of a defined challenge captured under stated conditions.</li><li><strong>Efficiency:</strong> a percentage that is meaningful only with particle size, challenge and test method.</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-muted" id="enquiry-checklist"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Technical note 02</p><h2>Filtration enquiry checklist</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Fluid name and complete composition</li><li>Normal and maximum temperature</li><li>Viscosity at filtration temperature</li><li>Batch volume or continuous flow</li><li>Solids concentration and particle information</li><li>Desired filtrate clarity or retention target</li><li>Existing filter type and housing model</li><li>Media dimensions and drawing</li><li>Clean and terminal differential pressure</li><li>Current grade and observed problem</li><li>Cleaning, sanitation or disposal method</li><li>Required certificates and declarations</li></ul></div></section>
$(Section 'Selection tools' 'Use the right technical landing page' (Cards -Items @(
@('01','Filter-pad guide','Cellulose purity, depth filtration, porosity, GSM, strength and trial design.','<a href="../filter-pads/index.html">Open filter-pad guide →</a>'),
@('02','Gelatin clarification','Temperature, viscosity, staged solids removal, yield and polishing.','<a href="../applications/gelatin-filtration.html">Open gelatin guide →</a>'),
@('03','Cartridge comparison','Pleated, spun, wound, steel and end-connection considerations.','<a href="../filter-cartridges/index.html">Compare cartridges →</a>'),
@('04','Quality documentation','How to define a useful grade and certificate package.','<a href="../about/quality.html">Review quality approach →</a>'),
@('05','Food & beverage','Clarification, sensory protection, yield and hygiene factors.','<a href="../applications/food-beverage-filtration.html">Read application guide →</a>'),
@('06','Chemical compatibility','A process-led framework for chemically demanding streams.','<a href="../applications/chemical-filtration.html">Read application guide →</a>')
)))
$(CTA 'Turn your operating data into a focused trial' 'Send the checklist with a current media sample, drawing or recent batch trend if available. This helps identify practical candidates without unsupported assumptions.')
"@
New-Page '/resources/' 'Industrial Filtration Resources | Sri Bharathi' 'Technical resources on depth filtration, filter pad selection, cartridge comparison, gelatin clarification and building a complete filter enquiry.' 'Industrial Filtration Resources' 'Engineering knowledge' 'Practical notes for engineers, purchase managers and plant teams evaluating depth pads, papers, cartridges and clarification systems.' $resourcesBody @(@('Home','/'),@('Resources','/resources/')) 'Article' 'Industrial Filtration Resources'

